 17592186045417] [17592186373018 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "98e43f2c-7032-55d3-ac19-6318a10d07a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373237 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373237 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79838" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373237 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373237 #edb/ref 1071 "Estimate $\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.5)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ at the point $(4,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373237 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba7d8609-104d-5a2e-b355-39ac5dc83584" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373237 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡y}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,\\text{d}x-\\sqrt{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x-2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4+Δx,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx-2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.5)=f(3.9,1.5),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3.9,1.5).$\n\nMoving from $(4,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $(3.9,1.5),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3.9-4=-0.1, \\\\ Δy & =1.5-\\frac{\\pi }{2}≈-0.070796.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (-0.1)-2(-0.070796) \\\\  & ≈0+0.141592 \\\\  & ≈0.141592.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141592.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.9,1.5) & ≈f(4,\\frac{\\pi }{2})+0.141592 \\\\ \\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1.5) & ≈\\sqrt{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+0.141592 \\\\  & ≈0+0.141592 \\\\  & ≈0.142,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186373241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373238 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b0095e22-2029-58c2-ab81-2e1546884b41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373239 #edb/ref 1080 "0.138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373239 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373239 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5523408e-53c1-55c6-9d6c-93f6067c5024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373240 #edb/ref 1080 "0.146" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373240 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373240 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a0e8bda-987d-556d-adc4-5475e67e3649" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373241 #edb/ref 1080 "0.142" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373241 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373241 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85457950-05dd-515a-979c-3c810b65e48e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373242 #edb/ref 1080 "0.144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e12f9b2-e25d-5e0c-8da0-288cbfb87a9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373243 #edb/ref 1080 "0.140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186373243 #edb/ref 